verdict.implementation_notes:
Approach. Add a client-side auto-purge pass in rizzy-client. A suggested signature is `VaultSync::auto_purge_due<R: CryptoRng>(&mut self, rng, unlocked, now_ms, retention_ms) -> Result<Vec<ItemId>, ClientError>` in crates/rizzy-client/src/items.rs. It would:
- iterate the merged items;
- for each, call `ItemMerge::purge_due(now_ms, retention_ms, self.holds_unapplied(id))`;
- issue `purge_item` (the existing lifecycle_op with Lifecycle::Purge) for each due item;
- use `rizzy_sync::merge::TRASH_RETENTION_MS` or `rizzy_core::item::display::DEFAULT_TRASH_RETENTION_MS` as the default retention.

The clock is still injected as now_ms, so the no-I/O rule holds. Run the pass after a successful sync/apply, while the vault is unlocked, so it happens only when a client is online. Callers to wire up:
- rizzy-wasm: add a method such as `autoPurge(now_ms)` in crates/rizzy-wasm/src/session.rs and device.rs, call it from packages/core's sync flow, and call it from the apps/web post-sync step.
- rizzy-cli: call it after `rv sync` (or on unlock+sync), and possibly offer a manual `rv trash purge-expired`.

The vault-settings item must never be auto-purged. It is never trashed, but guard it anyway.

Tests:
- rizzy-client/src/tests.rs, the ADR 0018 §12 unit test: no auto-purge while an unknown-version restore is parked. Hold the parked record, pass now >= trashed_at + 30 days, and assert there is no Purge op and the item is still Trashed.
- no purge before the retention period; purge at exactly trashed_at + retention;
- an item restored after being trashed is not purged;
- two devices auto-purging concurrently converge on one tombstone;
- a wasm/web test that the post-sync auto-purge runs.

Also update the ROADMAP/HANDOFF status text if it tracks progress. No ADR change is needed.

verdict.corrected_adr_gate:
needs_new_or_proposed_adr for the operator command. ADR 0031 (Accepted) authorizes retiring setups that are still held, with a successor, and nothing more. ADR 0003 is Partially superseded and cites §5.8 for rotation only. CRYPTO.md §5.8 states the goal ("admin marks the records invalid"), but it is not an ADR and names no mechanism. Several parts of a loss-recovery command are persistent-format and security-boundary decisions:
- marking credential records invalid or retiring an unknown setup in the database;
- recording a new setup next to orphaned records, with or without bypassing the NoRecordedSetup and SetupMismatch startup checks;
- handling sealed TOTP and login-state rows whose data_key_id is lost.

Under the CLAUDE.md ADR gate, all of that needs a new ADR, for example "Recovering from lost server secrets", drafted as Status: Proposed and approved by the owner before any code.

The self-hosting.md:211 correction is docs-only and needs no ADR: replace the false "no endpoint" reason with the true one, that the server refuses to start and no loss-recovery operator command exists.

verdict.implementation_notes:
Allowed now, as a docs-only change: fix docs/self-hosting.md:211. The endpoints exist (crates/rizzy-proto/src/http.rs:98-124). The real blocker is that `rizzy-vault` refuses to start without the matching secrets file (SetupMismatch, NoRecordedSetup and MissingDataKey in crates/rizzy-domain-auth/src/secrets.rs check_database), and no operator command exists for the loss case. Keep the warning that the age/gpg copy of secrets.json is the only working restore path.

Blocked until the owner accepts a new ADR (draft it Proposed from docs/adr/0000-template.md and add a row in docs/adr/README.md):
- **Command:** a `secrets recover-lost` style command, run with the server stopped, that:
  - writes a fresh secrets file with a new setup_id above every recorded one;
  - marks every recorded setup missing from the file as retired or lost in auth_opaque_setups, so its records take the fake-record path and the device or recovery path (ADR 0031 point 7);
  - drops pending login states;
  - deals with sealed TOTP rows under lost data keys, either by disabling TOTP for those accounts or by marking it re-enrolment-required. This is a security decision for the ADR.
- **Files:** crates/rizzy-server/src/cli.rs (parser and dispatch), crates/rizzy-domain-auth/src/secrets.rs (a startup-check variant or new SQL), the domain-auth SQL module, docs/self-hosting.md and docs/CRYPTO.md §5.8, which should name the command.
- **Tests:** integration tests for:
  - startup after recovery succeeds, and the old setup's accounts get the fake-record path at login;
  - an enrolled device can re-register through ACCOUNT_REREGISTER_START with a device session;
  - recovery through RECOVERY_* still works;
  - the command refuses when the current secrets file still matches;
  - the command is idempotent after a crash between the database step and the file step.

Also verify, which I have not done, that the reregister endpoint accepts a device-authenticated session for an account whose setup is retired.

verdict.corrected_adr_gate:
needs_new_or_proposed_adr. ADR 0021 is Partially superseded only in §9 by ADR 0032, so its §4 paging and covers rule is still binding. ADR 0018 is Accepted, and its §3 "Snapshots are claims" makes the merge cut a cover to the headers verified so far. Every fix changes a mechanism that one of these ADRs sets out:
(a) a wire or protocol paging rule, a change to ADR 0021 §4;
(b) the client carrying refused tombstone covers across pages, or re-merging them once the cut reaches the purge, which changes ADR 0018 §3 and ADR 0021 §4 cover semantics;
(c) a new snapshot field.
The test comment itself says it waits for the owner to "settle the rule". So no code change is allowed until the owner accepts a new ADR that supersedes ADR 0021 §4 (and ADR 0018 §3 if needed) in part. Drafting a Proposed ADR, if the owner asks for one, is allowed.
